{% if render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "thoughts" %}
{#
  To the Yield: what a duel in progress means, for the two fighters and for anyone watching.
  Renders nothing unless a duel is being fought: TTY_Main sets TTY_Status only then.
  It sits after 0200_combat_status on purpose: that one tells a badly hurt NPC "every hit could be
  fatal", which is not true in a duel. Facts only, never what the duel means: "formal", "nobody is
  meant to die" and "no shame" had NPCs judge a refused yield as cheating (seen live 2026-11-10).
  TTY_YieldRefused and TTY_ToTheDeath follow the fight, so the opponent's terms change with it.
#}
{% set duel = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", "none", "TTY_Status", "") %}
{% if duel != "" %}
{% set refused = papyrus_util("GetIntValue", "none", "TTY_YieldRefused", 0) %}
{% set death = papyrus_util("GetIntValue", "none", "TTY_ToTheDeath", 0) %}
{% if papyrus_util("GetIntValue", npc.UUID, "TTY_Opponent", 0) == 1 %}
- You are fighting a duel with {{ player.name }} right now, with weapons and magic, whatever each of you fights with, until someone goes down, or offers a yield and the other accepts it.{% if death != 1 %} A beaten fighter drops to their knees instead of dying.{% endif %} What this fight is to you is yours to decide, from who you are and who {{ player.name }} is to you. Keep words short, the way people talk mid-fight.
{% if death == 1 %}
- {{ player.name }} refused your yield and made this a fight to the death. Either of you can die now; nothing will stop it.
{% elif refused > 0 %}
- You offered your yield and {{ player.name }} refused it{% if refused > 1 %} ({{ refused }} times now){% endif %}. The fight goes on.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
- {{ duel }} You are watching, not fighting: a short remark at most, and do not join in.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{#
  NPC against NPC (TTY_NpcDuel). A challenge waiting on this NPC's answer comes first. A yield offered
  to a duelist asks for their answer the same way; TTY_NpcRefused counts on the one who offered it.
#}
{% if papyrus_util("GetIntValue", npc.UUID, "TTY_NpcChallenged", 0) == 1 %}
- ANSWER REQUIRED: {{ papyrus_util("GetStringValue", npc.UUID, "TTY_NpcChallengerName", "someone") }} has just challenged you to a duel: weapons and magic, whatever each of you fights with, until one of you yields or goes down. Answer now, in your own words: accept (AcceptDuel) or refuse (DeclineDuel).
{% endif %}
{#
  TTY_NpcStatus is set only while an NPC duel is being fought.
#}
{% set npcduel = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", "none", "TTY_NpcStatus", "") %}
{% if npcduel != "" %}
{% if papyrus_util("GetIntValue", npc.UUID, "TTY_NpcDuelist", 0) == 1 %}
{% set foe = papyrus_util("GetStringValue", npc.UUID, "TTY_NpcDuelFoe", "your opponent") %}
{% set ndeath = papyrus_util("GetIntValue", "none", "TTY_NpcToTheDeath", 0) %}
{% set nrefused = papyrus_util("GetIntValue", npc.UUID, "TTY_NpcRefused", 0) %}
- You are fighting a duel with {{ foe }} right now, with weapons and magic, whatever each of you fights with, until someone goes down, or offers a yield and the other accepts it.{% if ndeath != 1 %} A beaten fighter drops to their knees instead of dying.{% endif %} What this fight is to you is yours to decide, from who you are and who they are to you. Keep words short, the way people talk mid-fight.
{% if papyrus_util("GetIntValue", npc.UUID, "TTY_NpcYieldOffer", 0) == 1 %}
- ANSWER REQUIRED: {{ papyrus_util("GetStringValue", npc.UUID, "TTY_NpcYieldFrom", foe) }} has just offered you a yield. Answer now, in your own words: accept it (AcceptNpcYield), or refuse it and make them fight on (RefuseNpcYield){% if papyrus_util("GetIntValue", npc.UUID, "TTY_NpcDeathOK", 0) == 1 %}, or refuse it and make this a fight to the death (DeathNpcDuel){% endif %}.
{% elif ndeath == 1 %}
- This is a fight to the death now. Either of you can die; nothing will stop it.
{% elif nrefused > 0 %}
- You offered your yield and {{ foe }} refused it{% if nrefused > 1 %} ({{ nrefused }} times now){% endif %}. The fight goes on.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
- {{ npcduel }} You are watching, not fighting: a short remark at most, and do not join in.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
